# 21. Evidence Gaps

Several areas require deeper research before policy conclusions can be drawn.

### BLM

* frequency and geographic coverage of land-health evaluations;
* relationship between evaluations and subsequent management decisions;
* measurable ecological outcomes after grazing adjustments;
* effectiveness of restoration treatments;
* implementation of landscape-scale conservation measures.

### Forest Service

* relationship between forest-plan monitoring and actual plan revisions;
* treatment effectiveness;
* long-term watershed outcomes;
* wildlife response;
* post-fire ecological outcomes;
* interaction between timber, fuels, habitat, and resilience objectives.

### NPS

* frequency with which Vital Signs data changes management;
* examples of monitoring-triggered interventions;
* long-term ecological trends;
* management response to persistent negative trends.

### NWRS

* system-wide habitat-condition indicators;
* consistency of monitoring across refuges;
* species response to habitat restoration;
* long-term maintenance of restoration gains.

### Cross-agency

* landscape-scale governance;
* data interoperability;
* Tribal participation;
* private-land conservation;
* funding continuity;
* workforce capacity.

